@sponge225, a quick follow-up: I have updated this PR to the single-segment encoding approach suggested in #4334.

The revised implementation keeps each LangGraph key as one URI segment, translating encoded separators after percent-encoding (`%2F -> !s`, `%5C -> !b`). Literal `!` is still encoded as `%21`, so separator escapes remain distinct from literal key text.

I also added regression coverage for:
- leading, trailing, and repeated separators;
- backslashes, Unicode, dot segments, percent text, and literal `!s`/`!b`;
- the namespace/key identity collision identified during review;
- put/get/search/list/delete round trips.

Validation is green: 72 integration tests passed locally, CI is passing, and an exhaustive 66,430-key round-trip check found no collisions.

When convenient, could you please take another look? I’m happy to address any further feedback.
